At midday, Jonas and I take a break.
We go out onto the street.
We walk to a small bakery.
Many people are already waiting in the bakery.
Jonas orders his food first.
Then I order.
"What will you have?" the shop assistant asks.
"I will take a bread roll and a coffee, please," I answer.
"Would you like the bread roll with cheese?" he asks.
"Yes, very much," I say.
I pay for my lunch.
We take the food with us and go outside.
We eat together in front of the bakery.
The bread roll is really very crusty.
"How is your project going?" Jonas asks me.
"It is going well, but I am writing a lot of code today," I answer.
We talk a little more about work.
After half an hour we go back to the office.
In the afternoon, we continue working.
